  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Service-Disabled Veteran-Owned Small Business Set-Aside obligated $719M in FY2027 to date. The program produced 2,158 awards with an average award size of $333K. Obligations fell 92.9% year over year. The current-year total is partial because fiscal year totals are fiscal year to date. Obligations in the prior fiscal year were larger, with FY26 at $10.1B compared with FY27 at $719M. The Department of Veterans Affairs accounted for the bulk of current-year activity, obligating $672M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest industry by obligation in FY2027 to date at $191M, followed by Temporary Help Services at $72.3M and Other Computer Related Services at $72M. Top vendors in the current year include CITADEL FEDERAL SOLUTIONS LLC with $27.6M and VALIANT CONSTRUCTION LLC with $25.9M. These facts show where FY2027 to date buying is concentrated and the scale of awards being made so far this fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 92.9% year over year. FY26 obligations were $10.1B, while FY27 obligations are $719M in this fiscal year to date. AwardCount remained at 2,158 awards with an average award size of $333K in FY2027 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top buyers and industries in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $672M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $24.7M and the General Services Administration obligated $4.7M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest industry at $191M, followed by Temporary Help Services at $72.3M and Other Computer Related Services at $72M."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does the federal government award through SDVOSB set-asides?",
      "a": "The federal government awarded $719M through SDVOSB set-asides in FY2027 to date. The program issued 2,158 awards with an average award size of $333K. Obligations fell 92.9% year over year, down from FY26 obligations of $10.1B."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies use SDVOSB set-asides the most?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs used SDVOSB set-asides the most, obligating $672M in FY2027 to date. The Department of Homeland Security obligated $24.7M and the General Services Administration obligated $4.7M. Other agencies in the top ten include the Department of Transportation at $3.2M and the Department of Energy at $2.8M."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are the largest SDVOSB set-aside contractors?",
      "a": "CITADEL FEDERAL SOLUTIONS LLC is the largest SDVOSB set-aside contractor in FY2027 to date with $27.6M. VALIANT CONSTRUCTION LLC follows with $25.9M and DANIELS BUILDING CO INC follows with $23.4M. The top ten vendors also include STANDARD COMMUNICATIONS INC at $19.5M and JETT'S SPECIALTY CONTRACTING, LLC at $15.5M."
    }
